From 60298a709429377c3e0ac16f5d68a66f8f922856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:01:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] kcm_kwinoptions: one Form page, mouse actions on two
 sub-pages, no eager tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Note: on master this page is already QML (Kirigami.Form), not QtWidgets; the rework stays in QML.

Moved / renamed (config keys, kcfg and KWin reload signal unchanged):
- The tab bar Focus | Titlebar Actions | Window Actions | Movement & Placement is gone: the tabs were not peers.
  Main page now = focus and raising (first, untitled group), Placement, Snapping (was "Movement"), Overlay Positioning.
  Window Behavior.qml is Focus.qml + the groups of MovementAndPlacement.qml.
- Toolbar buttons "Titlebar Actions…" and "Window Actions…" push TitlebarActionsPage.qml / WindowActionsPage.qml.
- Group titles on those pages: "Titlebar Actions" -> "Titlebar" (it repeated the page title), "Maximize Button Actions" ->
  "Maximize Button", "Unfocused Inner Window Actions" -> "Unfocused Windows", "Inner Window, Titlebar, and Frame
  Actions" -> "Modifier Key". No "Advanced" anywhere.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-013/015 (long rare forms on named sub-pages), HIG-023, HIG-057. Page-design.md 1, 2, 6, 7.

Speed cause (code evidence): ui/main.qml put Focus, TitlebarActions, WindowActions and MovementAndPlacement in one
StackLayout, which instantiates every child up front: about 100 controls (ComboBoxes with JS model arrays,
SettingStateBindings, the OSD position selector) were built before the first frame although one tab is visible. Now
the first frame builds only the main form (about a third of them); the two action forms are created when opened
(kcm.push loads the page lazily). The C++ side has no blocking work (kwinoptions.cpp constructor only registers
settings).
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: Kirigami.Form as a child
of ColumnLayout with Layout.fillWidth (same shape as before, where the StackLayout sat in a ColumnLayout).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
